        'heading_path': list([
          'Request Body',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1,
        'page': None,
        'text': "When you need to send data from a client (let's say, a browser) to your API, you send it as a request body.",
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_67160b42939e',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Request Body',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 2,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'A request body is data sent by the client to your API. A response body is the data your API sends to the client.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_af4f27fcf48a',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Request Body',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 3,
        'page': None,
        'text': "Your API almost always has to send a response body. But clients don't necessarily need to send request bodies all the time, sometimes they only request a path, maybe with some query parameters, but don't send a body.",
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_ebbb916b48de',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Request Body',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
          dict({
            'href': 'https://pydantic.dev/docs/',
            'text': 'Pydantic',
          }),
        ]),
        'order': 4,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'To declare a request body, you use Pydantic models with all their power and benefits.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_a051cbd6849c',
        'data': dict({
          'kind': 'note',
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Request Body',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 5,
        'page': None,
        'text': "Note To send data, you should use one of: POST (the most common), PUT, DELETE or PATCH. Sending a body with a GET request has an undefined behavior in the specifications, nevertheless, it is supported by FastAPI, only for very complex/extreme use cases. As it is discouraged, the interactive docs with Swagger UI won't show the documentation for the body when using GET, and proxies in the middle might not support it.",
        'type': 'admonition',
      }),
