        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'First Steps',
          'OpenAPI',
          'What is OpenAPI for',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 39,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'The OpenAPI schema is what powers the two interactive documentation systems included.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_8eda10121fc9',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'First Steps',
          'OpenAPI',
          'What is OpenAPI for',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 40,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'And there are dozens of alternatives, all based on OpenAPI. You could easily add any of those alternatives to your application built with FastAPI.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_63853d29309e',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'First Steps',
          'OpenAPI',
          'What is OpenAPI for',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 41,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'You could also use it to generate code automatically, for clients that communicate with your API. For example, frontend, mobile or IoT applications.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_f1dd1f175a63',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'First Steps',
        ]),
        'level': 3,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 42,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Configure the app entrypoint in pyproject.toml',
        'type': 'heading',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_1397200943a3',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'First Steps',
          'Configure the app entrypoint in pyproject.toml',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 43,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'You can configure where your app is located in a pyproject.toml file like:',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_2ae568b414e3',
        'data': dict({
          'code': '''
            [tool.fastapi]
            entrypoint = "main:app"
  
          ''',
          'language': None,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'First Steps',
          'Configure the app entrypoint in pyproject.toml',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 44,
        'page': None,
        'text': '''
          [tool.fastapi]
          entrypoint = "main:app"
  
        ''',
        'type': 'code',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_8e8b1d1f3ba5',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'First Steps',
          'Configure the app entrypoint in pyproject.toml',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 45,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'That entrypoint will tell the fastapi command that it should import the app like:',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_a6d806f8170f',
        'data': dict({
          'code': '''
            from main import app
  
          ''',
          'language': None,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'First Steps',
          'Configure the app entrypoint in pyproject.toml',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 46,
        'page': None,
        'text': '''
          from main import app
  
        ''',
        'type': 'code',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_87711ce96100',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
