        ]),
        'order': 149,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Breaking Changes',
        'type': 'heading',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_6c4d33a5d349',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            '♻️ Refactor internals to preserve APIRouter and APIRoute instances. PR #15745 by @tiangolo.',
          ]),
          'ordered': False,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
          dict({
            'href': 'https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15745',
            'text': '#15745',
          }),
          dict({
            'href': 'https://github.com/tiangolo',
            'text': '@tiangolo',
          }),
        ]),
        'order': 150,
        'page': None,
        'text': '♻️ Refactor internals to preserve APIRouter and APIRoute instances. PR #15745 by @tiangolo.',
        'type': 'list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_ef446112faa7',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 151,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Unblocks ✨ SO MANY THINGS ✨',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_bcd4d1f6e3bc',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 152,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Before this, router.include_router(other_router) would take each path operation from other_router and "clone" it, or recreate it from scratch.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_4670d9cb2500',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 153,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'This would mean that in the end there was only one top level router, part of the app.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_1283f2092bd2',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 154,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'The way it is structured here is that there are a few additional classes to handle intermediate metadata for router and route inclusion. That way the information of "router X includes Y and Y includes Z" is stored somewhere, without affecting (recreating / cloning) the final route.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_a642c3110ea6',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': 4,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 155,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Non Objectives',
        'type': 'heading',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_372a9803b991',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
          'Non Objectives',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 156,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Dependencies for 404: previously I intended to support dependencies that would be executed even for 404, but that would conflict with the fact that a router could not find a match, but the next router did find a match. Executing dependencies in the router that did not find a match would not make sense, they could consume the request, body, etc. This original idea was discarded.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_d5017aef8928',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': 4,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 157,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Specific Breaking Changes',
        'type': 'heading',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_7e431c543b1f',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
          'Specific Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 158,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Now router.routes is no longer a plain list of APIRoute objects, it can contain these intermediate objects that can contain additional routers, forming a tree.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_af6d9e029d39',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
          'Specific Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 159,
        'page': None,
        'text': "Any logic that depended on iterating on the router.routes directly would be affected, that logic cannot expect to be able to extract data from a plain list of routes, as it's no longer a plain list but a tree.",
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_303bf9a59029',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
          'Specific Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 160,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Additionally, any logic that iterated on router.routes to modify them would now also see these new objects, and would not see all the routes in the app.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_ad0b2a208146',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
          'Specific Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 161,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'router.routes should be considered an internal implementation detail, only passed around to the FastAPI functions that need it.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_2c788ab9c279',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
        ]),
        'level': 4,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 162,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Features',
        'type': 'heading',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_295efdb79c81',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            'Adding routes (path operations) after a router is included now works, they are reflected as they are not copied.',
            'Including subrouter in mainrouter can be done before adding routes (path operations) to subrouter, because now the entire object is stored instead of copying the routes.',
            'As routes are not copied, in some cases that might save some memory.',
          ]),
          'ordered': False,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.137.0 (2026-06-14)',
          'Breaking Changes',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 163,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Adding routes (path operations) after a router is included now works, they are reflected as they are not copied. Including subrouter in mainrouter can be done before adding routes (path operations) to subrouter, because now the entire object is stored instead of copying the routes. As routes are not copied, in some cases that might save some memory.',
        'type': 'list',
