      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_4a60e5811e2e',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            '✨ Add support for shared/top-level parameters (dependencies, tags, etc). PR #2434 by @tiangolo.',
          ]),
          'ordered': False,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
          dict({
            'href': 'https://github.com/tiangolo/fastapi/pull/2434',
            'text': '#2434',
          }),
          dict({
            'href': 'https://github.com/tiangolo',
            'text': '@tiangolo',
          }),
        ]),
        'order': 1614,
        'page': None,
        'text': '✨ Add support for shared/top-level parameters (dependencies, tags, etc). PR #2434 by @tiangolo.',
        'type': 'list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_ecfafb16ec82',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1615,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Up to now, for several options, the only way to apply them to a group of path operations was in include_router. That works well, but the call to app.include_router() or router.include_router() is normally done in another file.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_155ea4d757c6',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1616,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'That means that, for example, to apply authentication to all the path operations in a router it would end up being done in a different file, instead of keeping related logic together.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_39591a5682d7',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1617,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Setting options in include_router still makes sense in some cases, for example, to override or increase configurations from a third party router included in an app. But in a router that is part of a bigger application, it would probably make more sense to add those settings when creating the APIRouter.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_e779e53b1b07',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1618,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'In FastAPI',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_879990b9a9d9',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1619,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'This allows setting the (mostly new) parameters (additionally to the already existing parameters):',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_3caac59dfad5',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            'default_response_class: updated to handle defaults in APIRouter and include_router.',
            'dependencies: to include ✨ top-level dependencies ✨ that apply to the whole application. E.g. to add global authentication.',
            'callbacks: OpenAPI callbacks that apply to all the path operations.',
            'deprecated: to mark all the path operations as deprecated. 🤷',
            'include_in_schema: to allow excluding all the path operations from the OpenAPI schema.',
            'responses: OpenAPI responses that apply to all the path operations.',
          ]),
          'ordered': False,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1620,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'default_response_class: updated to handle defaults in APIRouter and include_router. dependencies: to include ✨ top-level dependencies ✨ that apply to the whole application. E.g. to add global authentication. callbacks: OpenAPI callbacks that apply to all the path operations. deprecated: to mark all the path operations as deprecated. 🤷 include_in_schema: to allow excluding all the path operations from the OpenAPI schema. responses: OpenAPI responses that apply to all the path operations.',
        'type': 'list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_e3936d6fd2e0',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1621,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'For example:',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_07401d8ea527',
        'data': dict({
          'code': '''
            from fastapi import FastAPI, Depends
            
            
            async def some_dependency():
                return
            
            
            app = FastAPI(dependencies=[Depends(some_dependency)])
  
          ''',
          'language': None,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1622,
        'page': None,
        'text': '''
          from fastapi import FastAPI, Depends
          
          
          async def some_dependency():
              return
          
          
          app = FastAPI(dependencies=[Depends(some_dependency)])
  
        ''',
        'type': 'code',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_aa6feae8ce58',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1623,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'In APIRouter',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_879990b9a9d9_2',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1624,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'This allows setting the (mostly new) parameters (additionally to the already existing parameters):',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_1a83de5dabe1',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            "default_response_class: updated to handle defaults in APIRouter and include_router. For example, it's not needed to set it explicitly when creating callbacks.",
            'dependencies: to include ✨ router-level dependencies ✨ that apply to all the path operations in a router. Up to now, this was only possible with include_router.',
            'callbacks: OpenAPI callbacks that apply to all the path operations in this router.',
            'deprecated: to mark all the path operations in a router as deprecated.',
            'include_in_schema: to allow excluding all the path operations in a router from the OpenAPI schema.',
            'responses: OpenAPI responses that apply to all the path operations in a router.',
            'prefix: to set the path prefix for a router. Up to now, this was only possible when calling include_router.',
            'tags: OpenAPI tags to apply to all the path operations in this router.',
          ]),
          'ordered': False,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
          dict({
            'href': 'https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/openapi-callbacks/',
            'text': 'creating callbacks',
          }),
        ]),
        'order': 1625,
        'page': None,
        'text': "default_response_class: updated to handle defaults in APIRouter and include_router. For example, it's not needed to set it explicitly when creating callbacks. dependencies: to include ✨ router-level dependencies ✨ that apply to all the path operations in a router. Up to now, this was only possible with include_router. callbacks: OpenAPI callbacks that apply to all the path operations in this router. deprecated: to mark all the path operations in a router as deprecated. include_in_schema: to allow excluding all the path operations in a router from the OpenAPI schema. responses: OpenAPI responses that apply to all the path operations in a router. prefix: to set the path prefix for a router. Up to now, this was only possible when calling include_router. tags: OpenAPI tags to apply to all the path operations in this router.",
        'type': 'list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_e3936d6fd2e0_2',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1626,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'For example:',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_1a9c97757ed1',
        'data': dict({
          'code': '''
            from fastapi import APIRouter, Depends
            
            
            async def some_dependency():
                return
            
            
            router = APIRouter(prefix="/users", dependencies=[Depends(some_dependency)])
  
          ''',
          'language': None,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1627,
        'page': None,
        'text': '''
          from fastapi import APIRouter, Depends
          
          
          async def some_dependency():
              return
          
          
          router = APIRouter(prefix="/users", dependencies=[Depends(some_dependency)])
  
        ''',
        'type': 'code',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_df6bb35ad9cd',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1628,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'In include_router',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_43e60661fcd6',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1629,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Most of these settings are now supported in APIRouter, which normally lives closer to the related code, so it is recommended to use APIRouter when possible.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_736b179248f0',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1630,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'But include_router is still useful to, for example, add options (like dependencies, prefix, and tags) when including a third party router, or a generic router that is shared between several projects.',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_bfc224e50c62',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1631,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'This PR allows setting the (mostly new) parameters (additionally to the already existing parameters):',
        'type': 'paragraph',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_a4c5f1407a86',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            'default_response_class: updated to handle defaults in APIRouter and FastAPI.',
            'deprecated: to mark all the path operations in a router as deprecated in OpenAPI.',
            'include_in_schema: to allow disabling all the path operations from showing in the OpenAPI schema.',
            'callbacks: OpenAPI callbacks that apply to all the path operations in this router.',
          ]),
          'ordered': False,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
          '0.62.0 (2020-11-29)',
          'Features',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 1632,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'default_response_class: updated to handle defaults in APIRouter and FastAPI. deprecated: to mark all the path operations in a router as deprecated in OpenAPI. include_in_schema: to allow disabling all the path operations from showing in the OpenAPI schema. callbacks: OpenAPI callbacks that apply to all the path operations in this router.',
        'type': 'list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_3b947631eea8',
        'data': dict({
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Release Notes',
