        'order': 500,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'classmethod from_app(app, environ, buffered=False) Create a new response object from an application output. This works best if you pass it an application that returns a generator all the time. Sometimes applications may use the write() callable returned by the start_response function. This tries to resolve such edge cases automatically. But if you don’t get the expected output you should set buffered to True which enforces buffering.',
        'type': 'definition_list',
      }),
      dict({
