        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': 'If E is present and has a .keys() method, then does: for k in E.keys(): D[k] = E[k] If E is present and lacks a .keys() method, then does: for k, v in E: D[k] = v In either case, this is followed by: for k in F: D[k] = F[k]',
              'term': 'update([E, ]**F) → None. Update D from mapping/iterable E and F.',
            }),
          ]),
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'API',
          'Session Interface',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
          dict({
            'href': 'https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Any',
            'text': 'Any',
          }),
          dict({
            'href': 'https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Any',
            'text': 'Any',
          }),
          dict({
            'href': 'https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.NoReturn',
            'text': 'NoReturn',
          }),
        ]),
        'order': 625,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'update([E, ]**F) → None. Update D from mapping/iterable E and F. If E is present and has a .keys() method, then does: for k in E.keys(): D[k] = E[k] If E is present and lacks a .keys() method, then does: for k, v in E: D[k] = v In either case, this is followed by: for k in F: D[k] = F[k]',
        'type': 'definition_list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_cc324a601c50_4',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': '',
