            dict({
              'definition': 'Executes a function after this request. This is useful to modify response objects. The function is passed the response object and has to return the same or a new one. Example: This is more useful if a function other than the view function wants to modify a response. For instance think of a decorator that wants to add some headers without converting the return value into a response object. Changelog Added in version 0.9.',
