          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': 'Convert the class into a view function that can be registered for a route. By default, the generated view will create a new instance of the view class for every request and call its dispatch_request() method. If the view class sets init_every_request to False, the same instance will be used for every request. Except for name, all other arguments passed to this method are forwarded to the view class __init__ method. Changelog Changed in version 2.2: Added the init_every_request class attribute.',
