        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            "'?'. One argument will be consumed from the command line if possible, and produced as a single item. If no command-line argument is present, the value from default will be produced. Note that for optional arguments, there is an additional case - the option string is present but not followed by a command-line argument. In this case the value from const will be produced. Some examples to illustrate this: One of the more common uses of nargs='?' is to allow optional input and output files:",
          ]),
          'ordered': False,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
