        'order': 286,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'ArgumentParser.set_defaults(**kwargs) Most of the time, the attributes of the object returned by parse_args() will be fully determined by inspecting the command-line arguments and the argument actions. set_defaults() allows some additional attributes that are determined without any inspection of the command line to be added: Note that defaults can be set at both the parser level using set_defaults() and at the argument level using add_argument(). If both are called for the same argument, the last default set for an argument is used: Parser-level defaults can be particularly useful when working with multiple parsers. See the add_subparsers() method for an example of this type.',
        'type': 'definition_list',
      }),
