        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': 'Return True if cls is a subclass (direct, indirect, or virtual) of classinfo. A class is considered a subclass of itself. classinfo may be a tuple of class objects (or recursively, other such tuples) or a Union Type, in which case return True if cls is a subclass of any entry in classinfo. In any other case, a TypeError exception is raised. Changed in version 3.10: classinfo can be a Union Type.',
