        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': 'Compute a version of this path relative to the path represented by other. If it’s impossible, ValueError is raised: When walk_up is false (the default), the path must start with other. When the argument is true, .. entries may be added to form the relative path. In all other cases, such as the paths referencing different drives, ValueError is raised.: Warning This function is part of PurePath and works with strings. It does not check or access the underlying file structure. This can impact the walk_up option as it assumes that no symlinks are present in the path; call resolve() first if necessary to resolve symlinks. Changed in version 3.12: The walk_up parameter was added (old behavior is the same as walk_up=False). Deprecated since version 3.12, removed in version 3.14: Passing additional positional arguments is deprecated; if supplied, they are joined with other.',
              'term': 'PurePath.relative_to(other, walk_up=False)',
            }),
