        'block_id': 'b_a6be52431547',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': 'Make the path absolute, resolving any symlinks. A new path object is returned: “..” components are also eliminated (this is the only method to do so): If a path doesn’t exist or a symlink loop is encountered, and strict is True, OSError is raised. If strict is False, the path is resolved as far as possible and any remainder is appended without checking whether it exists. Changed in version 3.6: The strict parameter was added (pre-3.6 behavior is strict). Changed in version 3.13: Symlink loops are treated like other errors: OSError is raised in strict mode, and no exception is raised in non-strict mode. In previous versions, RuntimeError is raised no matter the value of strict.',
              'term': 'Path.resolve(strict=False)',
            }),
          ]),
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'pathlib — Object-oriented filesystem paths',
          'Concrete paths',
          'Expanding and resolving paths',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
