        'page': None,
        'text': 'Path.is_mount() Return True if the path is a mount point: a point in a file system where a different file system has been mounted. On POSIX, the function checks whether path’s parent, path/.., is on a different device than path, or whether path/.. and path point to the same i-node on the same device — this should detect mount points for all Unix and POSIX variants. On Windows, a mount point is considered to be a drive letter root (e.g. c:\\), a UNC share (e.g. \\\\server\\share), or a mounted filesystem directory. Added in version 3.7. Changed in version 3.12: Windows support was added.',
