        'order': 187,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Path.symlink_to(target, target_is_directory=False) Make this path a symbolic link pointing to target. On Windows, a symlink represents either a file or a directory, and does not morph to the target dynamically. If the target is present, the type of the symlink will be created to match. Otherwise, the symlink will be created as a directory if target_is_directory is true or a file symlink (the default) otherwise. On non-Windows platforms, target_is_directory is ignored. Note The order of arguments (link, target) is the reverse of os.symlink()’s. Changed in version 3.13: Raises UnsupportedOperation if os.symlink() is not available. In previous versions, NotImplementedError was raised.',
        'type': 'definition_list',
