              'definition': 'Content of the response, in unicode. If Response.encoding is None, encoding will be guessed using charset_normalizer or chardet. The encoding of the response content is determined based solely on HTTP headers, following RFC 2616 to the letter. If you can take advantage of non-HTTP knowledge to make a better guess at the encoding, you should set r.encoding appropriately before accessing this property.',
