        'order': 148,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'class requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter(pool_connections: int = 10, pool_maxsize: int = 10, max_retries: int | Retry = 0, pool_block: bool = False)[source] The built-in HTTP Adapter for urllib3. Provides a general-case interface for Requests sessions to contact HTTP and HTTPS urls by implementing the Transport Adapter interface. This class will usually be created by the Session class under the covers. Usage:',
        'type': 'definition_list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_121c4954a0de_2',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': '',
              'term': 'Parameters:',
            }),
          ]),
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Developer Interface',
          'Lower-Lower-Level Classes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 149,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'Parameters:',
        'type': 'definition_list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_87744a92bddd',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            'pool_connections – The number of urllib3 connection pools to cache.',
            'pool_maxsize – The maximum number of connections to save in the pool.',
            'max_retries – The maximum number of retries each connection should attempt. Note, this applies only to failed DNS lookups, socket connections and connection timeouts, never to requests where data has made it to the server. By default, Requests does not retry failed connections. If you need granular control over the conditions under which we retry a request, import urllib3’s Retry class and pass that instead.',
            'pool_block – Whether the connection pool should block for connections.',
          ]),
          'ordered': False,
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Developer Interface',
          'Lower-Lower-Level Classes',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 150,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'pool_connections – The number of urllib3 connection pools to cache. pool_maxsize – The maximum number of connections to save in the pool. max_retries – The maximum number of retries each connection should attempt. Note, this applies only to failed DNS lookups, socket connections and connection timeouts, never to requests where data has made it to the server. By default, Requests does not retry failed connections. If you need granular control over the conditions under which we retry a request, import urllib3’s Retry class and pass that instead. pool_block – Whether the connection pool should block for connections.',
        'type': 'list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_4f5b5c4c76c3',
        'data': dict({
          'code': '''
            >>> import requests
            >>> s = requests.Session()
            >>> a = requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter(max_retries=3)
            >>> s.mount('http://', a)
  
          ''',
          'language': None,
        }),
