        'order': 209,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'class requests.cookies.RequestsCookieJar(policy=None)[source] Compatibility class; is a http.cookiejar.CookieJar, but exposes a dict interface. This is the CookieJar we create by default for requests and sessions that don’t specify one, since some clients may expect response.cookies and session.cookies to support dict operations. Requests does not use the dict interface internally; it’s just for compatibility with external client code. All requests code should work out of the box with externally provided instances of CookieJar, e.g. LWPCookieJar and FileCookieJar. Unlike a regular CookieJar, this class is pickleable. Warning dictionary operations that are normally O(1) may be O(n).',
        'type': 'definition_list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_58e19c2147ec',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': 'Add correct Cookie: header to request (urllib.request.Request object). The Cookie2 header is also added unless policy.hide_cookie2 is true.',
              'term': 'add_cookie_header(request)',
            }),
          ]),
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Developer Interface',
          'Cookies',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 210,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'add_cookie_header(request) Add correct Cookie: header to request (urllib.request.Request object). The Cookie2 header is also added unless policy.hide_cookie2 is true.',
        'type': 'definition_list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_3b4849dfba97',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': 'Clear some cookies. Invoking this method without arguments will clear all cookies. If given a single argument, only cookies belonging to that domain will be removed. If given two arguments, cookies belonging to the specified path within that domain are removed. If given three arguments, then the cookie with the specified name, path and domain is removed. Raises KeyError if no matching cookie exists.',
              'term': 'clear(domain=None, path=None, name=None)',
            }),
          ]),
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Developer Interface',
          'Cookies',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 211,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'clear(domain=None, path=None, name=None) Clear some cookies. Invoking this method without arguments will clear all cookies. If given a single argument, only cookies belonging to that domain will be removed. If given two arguments, cookies belonging to the specified path within that domain are removed. If given three arguments, then the cookie with the specified name, path and domain is removed. Raises KeyError if no matching cookie exists.',
        'type': 'definition_list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_0cc518a6161d',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': 'Discard all expired cookies. You probably don’t need to call this method: expired cookies are never sent back to the server (provided you’re using DefaultCookiePolicy), this method is called by CookieJar itself every so often, and the .save() method won’t save expired cookies anyway (unless you ask otherwise by passing a true ignore_expires argument).',
              'term': 'clear_expired_cookies()',
            }),
          ]),
        }),
        'heading_path': list([
          'Developer Interface',
          'Cookies',
        ]),
        'level': None,
        'links': list([
        ]),
        'order': 212,
        'page': None,
        'text': 'clear_expired_cookies() Discard all expired cookies. You probably don’t need to call this method: expired cookies are never sent back to the server (provided you’re using DefaultCookiePolicy), this method is called by CookieJar itself every so often, and the .save() method won’t save expired cookies anyway (unless you ask otherwise by passing a true ignore_expires argument).',
        'type': 'definition_list',
      }),
      dict({
        'block_id': 'b_ab6343221ac4',
        'data': dict({
          'items': list([
            dict({
              'definition': 'Discard all session cookies. Note that the .save() method won’t save session cookies anyway, unless you ask otherwise by passing a true ignore_discard argument.',
              'term': 'clear_session_cookies()',
            }),
          ]),
